        "content": "**Spring AI** is a Spring Framework project for building AI-enabled Java applications using familiar Spring patterns and abstractions. It helps integrate generative AI models without tying application code too closely to a specific provider.

### Key capabilities

- **Model support:** Integrations with providers such as OpenAI, Microsoft Azure OpenAI, Amazon Bedrock, Google Vertex AI, Anthropic, Ollama, and others.
- **Portable APIs:** Common interfaces for chat, text, image, audio, embedding, and moderation models where supported.
- **`ChatClient`:** A fluent API for prompts, model responses, streaming, advisors, and structured output.
- **Tool calling:** Lets models invoke Java methods or external services to retrieve data or perform actions.
- **RAG:** Retrieval-Augmented Generation support, including document ingestion, text splitting, embeddings, vector stores, and retrieval advisors.
- **Vector databases:** Integrations with stores such as PostgreSQL/PGvector, Redis, Elasticsearch, MongoDB Atlas, Milvus, Neo4j, Pinecone, Qdrant, and others.
- **Structured output:** Maps model responses into Java classes and other structured types.
- **Conversation memory:** Advisors and repositories for retaining chat context.
- **Observability:** Metrics and tracing integration through Spring Boot and Micrometer.
- **Spring Boot starters:** Auto-configuration and externalized configuration for supported model providers and vector stores.
- **MCP support:** Integration with the Model Context Protocol for connecting AI applications to tools and resources.

A small conceptual example:

```java
@RestController
class AiController {

    private final ChatClient chatClient;

    AiController(ChatClient.Builder builder) {
        this.chatClient = builder.build();
    }

    @GetMapping("/ask")
    String ask(@RequestParam String question) {
        return chatClient.prompt()
                .user(question)
                .call()
                .content();
    }
}
```

You would add the appropriate Spring AI model starter and configure the provider’s API key and model in `application.properties` or `application.yml`.

Official documentation:

- [Spring AI project page](https://spring.io/projects/spring-ai)
- [Spring AI reference documentation](https://docs.spring.io/spring-ai/reference/)
- [Spring AI GitHub repository](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-ai)",
